# Send a prompt to the local LLM and get its reply.
# The model name is a node parameter — the caller only supplies the question.
string prompt
# "" = use the llm node's own persona (it owns how the robot talks). Set this to
# turn the node into a classifier instead: name the exact labels you will accept.
string system
---
# "" means no usable answer: LLM unreachable, timed out, or it said nothing.
# The reason is logged by the llm node, callers just fall back to a canned line.
# Classifier callers must also treat "not one of my labels" as a fallback — an
# LLM answers off-menu now and then, no matter how firm the system prompt is.
string response
